,-0.01784621551632881,0.01286537665873766,-0.0945519283413887,0.047960903495550156,-0.07570774108171463,0.028857337310910225,-0.036932092159986496,-0.05675670877099037],"environment_constraints":{"dependencies":{},"markers":{"memory_write_only":"true","retrieval_performed":"false"},"runtime":"docker","versions":{"python":"3.12.1"}},"evidence_count":1,"evidence_summary":"A test run of pytest failed with exit code 1. The subsequent recovery edited the file to reorder statements, defining the variable before checking its attributes, after which the test succeeded with exit code 0.","guidance":"When a function references a variable in a check before the variable is assigned, move the assignment before the check to ensure the variable is defined when used.","id":"recovery-pattern-f490f62ab931191c6eac6db1","invalidated_at":null,"source_chronological_index":3,"source_failure_id":"ec4d135c-2a26-5797-9c45-b7361966bf12","source_failure_type":"test_failure","source_operation":"run_command","source_outcome_id":"100e1818-1642-5aee-8940-3508d5b62202","source_resolution_id":"c518e18b-2830-5e05-8ba8-5972114f281e","source_task_id":"GS-T003","source_tool":"run_command","title":"Reorder variable definitions to avoid UnboundLocalError","trigger":{"failure_context":"frozen objective failed before agent execution","failure_signature":"run_command:exit_code=1","failure_type":"test_failure","source_action_arguments":{"command":["python","-m","pytest"]},"source_operation":"run_command","source_task_problem_statement":"prime_meridian function raises UnboundLocalError when axes frame lacks observer\r\n\r\n#### Description\r\n\r\nThe `prime_meridian` function in `sunpy.visualization.drawing` raises an `UnboundLocalError` instead of the expected `ValueError` when the coordinate frame of the WCSAxes does not have an observer.\r\n\r\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport sunpy.visualization.drawing as drawing\r\nfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\r\nfrom astropy.wcs import WCS\r\n\r\naxes = Figure().add_subplot(projection=WCS())\r\ndrawing.prime_meridian(axes)\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Expected behavior\r\nShould raise a `ValueError` with message about the coordinate frame not having an observer.\r\n\r\n#### Actual behavior\r\nRaises `UnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable \u0027axes_frame\u0027 where it is not associated with a value`\r\n\r\nThe function appears to be checking for the observer attribute before `axes_frame` is defined, causing the variable to be referenced before assignment.","source_tool":"run_command","version_sensitive":true},"verification_status":"observed_successful","embedding_dimension":384}
