de is completely missing. This makes the output much harder to read as all code appears as plain text without any color or formatting.\r\n\r\n## Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport stackprinter\r\n\r\n# Set up stackprinter\r\nstackprinter.set_excepthook()\r\n\r\n# Trigger an exception to see the formatted output\r\ndef problematic_function():\r\n    return 1/0\r\n\r\nproblematic_function()\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nThe source code in the stack trace should be syntax highlighted, with different colors for keywords, variables, strings, etc. making it easier to read the code context.\r\n\r\n## Actual Behavior\r\n\r\nAll source code appears as plain text without any syntax highlighting. The output is just raw text without any formatting applied to different code elements.\r\n\r\nThis seems to be related to the source annotation functionality which should be parsing the source code into tokens and applying appropriate formatting, but it\u0027s not working correctly.\r\n\r\nI noticed this issue after updating to the latest version. The previous version had proper syntax highlighting that made stack traces much more readable.","source_tool":"run_command","version_sensitive":true},"verification_status":"observed_successful","embedding_dimension":384}
